Paladins~

COPY~Rylorn\Items\clesfire.itm~ ~override\clesfire.itm~
SAY NAME1~Celestial Fire~
SAY NAME2~Celestial Fire~
SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC~"Celestial Fire" is the only object that Trias has left to remind him of the Upper Planes. This heavy blade is warm to the touch, and flames have been carved across the surface of the blade. The intricacy of the carvings is breathtaking; they are done with such skill that the sword seems to be burning with metallic flames... someone must have spent several centuries rendering them. The metal of the blade is unfamiliar... it is heavy, but it shines like silver. The sword looks several millennia old. A faint hum can be felt within it, and the vibration becomes stronger when it touches human flesh. Not surprisingly, "Celestial Fire" can be wielded only by those with sufficient strength and purity of heart. When used in combat, "Celestial Fire" bursts into a holy radiance that burns any evil creature it strikes in combat.

STATISTICS:
Damage: 3-18 Slashing
Enchanted: +2
Special:
   +2 to Armor Class
   +10 Fire Damage
   +10% Resistance to Slashing Attacks
THAC0: +2
Speed: 3
Weight: 5
Proficiency: Long sword
Only usable by:
Lawful Good characters~

COPY~Rylorn\Items\cyricnec.itm~ ~override\cyricnec.itm~
SAY NAME1~Cyric's Necklace~
SAY NAME2~Cyric's Necklace~
SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC~This necklace radiates a faint chill. A powerful Anti-Magic Aura around this amulet makes it useful against any magic user

STATISTICS:
15% Magic Resistance

Useable by:
Everyone~
COPY~Rylorn\Items\dakleat0.itm~ ~override\dakleat0.itm~
SAY NAME1~DAK'KON'S ZERTH ARMOR~
SAY NAME2~DAK'KON'S ZERTH ARMOR~
SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC~Dak'kon's ceremonial zerth armor. It is fashioned of interlocking metal rings, formed of the same substance that Dak'kon's blade is made of. (Unlike the blade, however, it does not appear that the armor changes based on the mental state of the wielder.) The armor is worn over a padded red tunic, and spiked bracers and shoulder pads have been added to give greater protection to the arms and upper body. While Dak'kon's armor is similar to chain mail, it is lighter and more flexible, allowing him to wield his sword more effectively. It seems that when the sword and armor are used in tandem, the armor actually becomes lighter in weight and more flexible, more like cloth than chain mail. Whether this is a unique property of karach, or whether this is some magical effect of the two items, is unknown.

STATISTICS:
Armor Class: 5
Weight: 25~

